name libgreek
category Package
revision 65004
shortdesc Greek letters in math mode from Libertinus or Linux Libertine/Biolinum
relocated 1
longdesc This package allows LaTeX users (especially if using
longdesc traditional LaTeX/pdfLaTeX) to set the Greek letters in math
longdesc mode to use the glyphs from the Libertinus Serif or Sans font,
longdesc via the font support files provided by the libertinus-type1
longdesc package of Bob Tennent. All Greek letters are defined both in
longdesc \...up and \...it variants. The style (ISO, TeX, or French i.
longdesc e. upright) can be modified midway in the document. A "legacy"
longdesc mode uses font support from the (obsolete) package
longdesc https://ctan.org/pkg/libertine-legacy which map to the Linux
longdesc Libertine or Biolinum fonts. This package is for users which
longdesc only want to customize Greek letters in math mode.
runfiles size=8
 RELOC/tex/latex/libgreek/libgreek-legacy.sty
 RELOC/tex/latex/libgreek/libgreek.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/libgreek
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics font-maths font-supp
catalogue-version 1.1
